Copyright (c) 2026 clixmods. All rights reserved, except as granted below.

This license covers everything in this repository and in the official releases:
the mod, the data pack, the textures and every other file (the "Software").

"Owner" is clixmods. "Official Repository" is the repository that the Owner names as
such in the README and in the project pages on Modrinth and CurseForge. "Official
Release" is a jar or a data pack zip published by the Owner, unmodified.

1. What you may do

   a. Read the source code, and build the Software for your own use.
   b. Run the Software, alone or in a modpack, on your own machine or on a server.
   c. Modify the Software privately, to study it, to test it or to prepare a
      contribution under section 3.
   d. Redistribute an Official Release, unchanged, in a modpack or on a mirror, as long
      as you give the credit described in section 4.

2. What you may not do

   a. Publish, upload or distribute a modified version of the Software, or a fork of
      the Official Repository, by any means, except as allowed by section 5.
   b. Copy code, textures or other files of the Software into another project.
   c. Present the Software as your own work, or as approved by the Owner when it is not.
   d. Remove or alter the copyright notices, the license, or the credits shipped with
      the Software.

3. Contributions

   Contributions are made as pull requests to the Official Repository, and nowhere else.
   By submitting one, you confirm that you wrote it or have the right to submit it, and
   you grant the Owner a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, irrevocable and
   sublicensable license to use, modify, distribute and relicense it, as part of the
   Software or on its own, under this license or any other. You keep your own copyright.
   The Owner may accept or refuse any contribution. Every contributor whose
   contribution is accepted is credited in the Software (a credits file shipped with
   it), and this credit stays whatever happens to the project: a change of license,
   the abandonment described in section 5, or a fork. It cannot be removed.

4. Credit

   Wherever you redistribute an Official Release, you must:

   a. name the project ("Living Horizon") and its author (clixmods);
   b. link to the Official Repository, in a visible place such as the modpack
      description or its credits file;
   c. keep every credit and notice that ships with the Software;
   d. not suggest that the Owner made, endorses or supports your distribution.

5. When the project is abandoned

   The Owner declares the project abandoned by archiving the Official Repository, or by
   saying so in its README. From that moment, and for the versions of the Software that
   exist at that moment, this license is replaced by the GNU General Public License
   version 3 (GPL-3.0-only), with these additional terms, as allowed by its section 7:

   a. Anyone may fork and carry the project on, under the GPL.
   b. A fork must say clearly, in its README and on its project pages, that it is an
      unofficial continuation of Living Horizon, and link to the original repository.
   c. A fork must keep the copyright notices and every credit of the original, including
      all contributors of the original project, and add its own contributors beside them.
   d. A fork must not use the name "Living Horizon" or the logo as its own, nor suggest
      that it is the original project.

   Work published by the Owner after the abandonment stays under the license the Owner
   chooses.

